<title>SWEDEN: Skandia says AFS sold for $1 bln so far in 1997.</title>
<headline>Skandia says AFS sold for $1 bln so far in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurer Skandia said on Monday sales for its U.S. unit linked division Skandia Assurance &amp; Financial Service (AFS) totalled $1 billion so far in 1997.</p>
<p>The figure compares to $652 million in the corresponding year-earlier period ending in mid-April.</p>
<p>AFS sold unit linked insurances for $2.8 billion in 1996, Skandia said in a statement.</p>
<p>The subsidiary currently manages a total of $8.5 billion, the company added.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
